Yes, I have reproduced this bug using a debug texture, which more clearly illustrates this issue:
![panorama_image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0a7ab40b-41f7-43cc-9b3d-2c5f023f76b5)

The result indicates that the skybox and the environment map are rotated in opposite directions:
<img width="1281" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9b42ac19-2e93-4114-aa7f-135cc44bbc34">

I found some clues here: "Cube maps are left-handed so we negate the z coordinate" (https://www.khronos.org/opengl/wiki/Cubemap_Texture)
```wgsl
@fragment
fn skybox_fragment(in: VertexOutput) -> @location(0) vec4<f32> {
    let ray_direction = coords_to_ray_direction(in.position.xy, view.viewport);

    // Cube maps are left-handed so we negate the z coordinate.
    let out = textureSample(skybox, skybox_sampler, ray_direction * vec3(1.0, 1.0, -1.0));
    return vec4(out.rgb * uniforms.brightness, out.a);
}
```

For the skybox cubemap, we rotate the ray in a right-handed view space coordinate, while for the environment map, we rotate it in a right-handed world space coordinate. However, there appears to be a difference between these two types of cubemaps. I will do some research to figure it out.

I've identified the issue: In the environment map, I initially inverted the z before transforming, which placed the transformation in a left-handed coordinate system. I should transform first, like with the skybox, and then invert the z. 😄

```wgsl
if (!found_diffuse_indirect) {
    // The inversion should occur after the transformation.
    var irradiance_sample_dir = vec3(N.xy, -N.z);
    // Rotating the world space ray direction by the environment light map transform matrix, it is 
    // equivalent to rotating the diffuse environment cubemap itself.
    irradiance_sample_dir = (environment_map_uniform.transform * vec4(irradiance_sample_dir, 1.0)).xyz;
    radiances.irradiance = textureSampleLevel(
            bindings::diffuse_environment_maps[query_result.texture_index],
            bindings::environment_map_sampler,
            irradiance_sample_dir,
            0.0).rgb * query_result.intensity;
}
```

The correct version:

```wgsl
if (!found_diffuse_indirect) {
    var irradiance_sample_dir = N;
    // Rotating the world space ray direction by the environment light map transform matrix, it is 
    // equivalent to rotating the diffuse environment cubemap itself.
    irradiance_sample_dir = (environment_map_uniform.transform * vec4(irradiance_sample_dir, 1.0)).xyz;
    // Cube maps are left-handed so we negate the z coordinate.
    irradiance_sample_dir.z = -irradiance_sample_dir.z;
    radiances.irradiance = textureSampleLevel(
            bindings::diffuse_environment_maps[query_result.texture_index],
            bindings::environment_map_sampler,
            irradiance_sample_dir,
            0.0).rgb * query_result.intensity;
}
```

I will resolve all the aforementioned issues above in the upcoming commits today.

@alice-i-cecile @Azorlogh I apologize for the mistake that led to the mismatch of the mesh view bindings. I should have conducted more thorough testing before submiting these changes. I have now resolved all the issues and tested numerous examples. Below is a summary of the code changes.

1. The `EnvironmentMapUniform` should be configured as a per-view buffer, therefore I have modified the uniform to use a dynamic offset. We also need to include the `ViewEnvironmentMapUniformOffset` in all the associated `ViewNode`s and `RenderCommand`s.
    ```rust
    uniform_buffer::<EnvironmentMapUniform>(true).visibility(ShaderStages::FRAGMENT)
    ```

2. Some of the camera may not contain a `EnvironmentMapLight`, so we need to fallback to a default binding for the `EnvironmentMapUniform`
    ```rust
    fn gather_environment_map_uniform(
        view_query: Extract<Query<(Entity, Option<&EnvironmentMapLight>), With<Camera3d>>>,
        mut commands: Commands,
    ) {
        for (view_entity, environment_map_light) in view_query.iter() {
            let environment_map_uniform = if let Some(environment_map_light) = environment_map_light {
                EnvironmentMapUniform {
                    transform: Transform::from_rotation(environment_map_light.rotation)
                        .compute_matrix()
                        .inverse(),
                }
            } else {
                EnvironmentMapUniform::default()
            };
            commands
                .get_or_spawn(view_entity)
                .insert(environment_map_uniform);
        }
    }
    ```

3. Changing the binding number in `mesh_view_bindings.wgsl` and `mesh_view_bindings.rs` is insufficient; the tone mapping LUT bindings also required adjustment. Since these numbers are injected through shader definitions, they are easily overloooked. **This is the root cause of this issue**.
    ```rust
    #define_import_path bevy_core_pipeline::tonemapping_lut_bindings
    
    @group(0) @binding(#TONEMAPPING_LUT_TEXTURE_BINDING_INDEX) var dt_lut_texture: texture_3d<f32>;
    @group(0) @binding(#TONEMAPPING_LUT_SAMPLER_BINDING_INDEX) var dt_lut_sampler: sampler;
    ```
    
    ```
    diff --git a/crates/bevy_pbr/src/render/mesh.rs b/crates/bevy_pbr/src/render/mesh.rs
    index 8432cbd97..282b116e9 100644
    --- a/crates/bevy_pbr/src/render/mesh.rs
    +++ b/crates/bevy_pbr/src/render/mesh.rs
    @@ -1765,11 +1765,11 @@ impl SpecializedMeshPipeline for MeshPipeline {
                 shader_defs.push("TONEMAP_IN_SHADER".into());
                 shader_defs.push(ShaderDefVal::UInt(
                     "TONEMAPPING_LUT_TEXTURE_BINDING_INDEX".into(),
    -                20,
    +                21,
                 ));
                 shader_defs.push(ShaderDefVal::UInt(
                     "TONEMAPPING_LUT_SAMPLER_BINDING_INDEX".into(),
    -                21,
    +                22,
                 ));
    ```
